{"type":"message","id":"0f4af4a0","parentId":"6c5f43e5","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:38.950Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fix the data extraction/storage bug in Biomed BorBor at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/\n\n## The Problem\nThe LLM conversation layer (src/services/llm-conversation.js) handles user chat beautifully, but the structured data logging to SQLite is broken. The webhook route (src/routes/webhook.js) feeds user messages to both the LLM and the tree engine, and the tree engine stores data in wrong fields.\n\nExample from a real conversation:\n- User said \"It's making a weird noise!\" when asked for brand → got stored as equipment_brand\n- Equipment type, brand, and symptom fields are all jumbled\n\n## Root Cause\nIn src/routes/webhook.js, the handleWithLLM function:\n1. Sends user input to LLM → LLM responds naturally AND may return a treeAction\n2. If treeAction exists: feeds treeAction to handleIncomingMessage (good)\n3. If NO treeAction: feeds RAW user input to handleIncomingMessage (BAD — raw text goes into wrong tree state)\n\nThe tree engine (conversationEngine.js) is a state machine. When it receives input it doesn't understand at a particular state, it falls through to fuzzy matching and may store the raw text in whatever field that state expects.\n\n## The Fix\n\n### Approach: Make the LLM extract structured data AND manage conversation naturally\n\nModify src/services/llm-conversation.js to:\n\n1. **Always extract structured data** from the conversation. Update the system prompt to instruct the LLM to return structured JSON with ALL relevant fields it can extract from the message, not just tree actions.\n\n2. **Change the JSON response format** to:\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"tree_input\" | \"register\" | \"update_issue\" | \"none\",\n  \"value\": \"matched tree option if applicable\",\n  \"extracted\": {\n    \"name\": \"Doug\",\n    \"facility\": \"Koidu Government Hospital\",\n    \"equipment_type\": \"oxygen_concentrator\",\n    \"brand\": \"AirSep\",\n    \"symptom\": \"loud grinding noise\",\n    \"model\": null\n  }\n}\n```\n\n3. **Add a data sync function** that takes the extracted fields and updates the database directly, bypassing the tree engine's state machine for data storage:\n\n```javascript\nfunction syncExtractedData(phone, extracted) {\n  const db = getDb();\n  const tech = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM technicians WHERE phone = ?').get(phone);\n  if (!tech) return;\n  \n  // Update technician name\n  if (extracted.name && !tech.name) {\n    db.prepare('UPDATE technicians SET name = ? WHERE phone = ?').run(extracted.name, phone);\n  }\n  \n  // Update facility\n  if (extracted.facility) {\n    const facility = db.prepare('SELECT id FROM facilities WHERE name LIKE ?').get('%' + extracted.facility + '%');\n    if (facility && !tech.facility_id) {\n      db.prepare('UPDATE technicians SET facility_id = ? WHERE phone = ?').run(facility.id, phone);\n    }\n  }\n  \n  // Update current issue\n  const conv = db.prepare('SELECT current_issue_id FROM conversations WHERE phone = ?').get(phone);\n  if (conv?.current_issue_id) {\n    const issue = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM issues WHERE id = ?').get(conv.current_issue_id);\n    if (issue) {\n      if (extracted.equipment_type) {\n        // Map to valid equipment type\n        const typeMap = {\n          'oxygen concentrator': 'oxygen_concentrator', 'o2 concentrator': 'oxygen_concentrator',\n          'autoclave': 'autoclave', 'sterilizer': 'autoclave',\n          'centrifuge': 'centrifuge',\n          'infant incubator': 'infant_incubator', 'incubator': 'infant_incubator',\n          'patient monitor': 'patient_monitor', 'monitor': 'patient_monitor',\n          'suction machine': 'suction_machine', 'suction': 'suction_machine',\n        };\n        const mapped = typeMap[extracted.equipment_type.toLowerCase()] || extracted.equipment_type;\n        db.prepare('UPDATE issues SET equipment_type = ? WHERE id = ?').run(mapped, issue.id);\n      }\n      if (extracted.brand && issue.equipment_brand !== extracted.brand) {\n        db.prepare('UPDATE issues SET equipment_brand = ? WHERE id = ?').run(extracted.brand, issue.id);\n      }\n      if (extracted.symptom) {\n        db.prepare('UPDATE issues SET failure_description = ? WHERE id = ?').run(extracted.symptom, issue.id);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n4. **Call syncExtractedData** after every LLM response, regardless of whether there's a tree action.\n\n### Modify the system prompt in buildSystemPrompt():\n\nAdd to the response format instructions:\n```\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\nAlways start your response with a JSON line containing:\n{\"action\": \"tree_input\", \"value\": \"<option>\", \"extracted\": {\"name\": \"...\", \"facility\": \"...\", \"equipment_type\": \"...\", \"brand\": \"...\", \"symptom\": \"...\", \"model\": \"...\"}}\n\nThe \"extracted\" object should contain ANY information you can identify from the conversation so far:\n- name: the technician's name if they've mentioned it\n- facility: the health facility name\n- equipment_type: one of: oxygen concentrator, autoclave, centrifuge, infant incubator, patient monitor, suction machine\n- brand: equipment brand/manufacturer (DeVilbiss, AirSep, Longfian, Canta, BPL, Tuttnauer, Prestige Medical, Edan, etc.)\n- symptom: the main problem described (e.g., \"loud grinding noise\", \"won't start\", \"low oxygen output\")\n- model: specific model number if mentioned\n\nOnly include fields you're confident about. Use null for unknown fields.\n```\n\n### Modify handleWithLLM in src/routes/webhook.js:\n\nAfter getting the LLM response, call syncExtractedData with whatever was extracted:\n```javascript\nasync function handleWithLLM(phone, input) {\n  try {\n    const { llmResponse, treeAction, extracted } = await processWithLLM(phone, input);\n    \n    // Always sync extracted data to DB\n    if (extracted) {\n      syncExtractedData(phone, extracted);\n    }\n    \n    // Rest of the handler...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Modify processWithLLM return value:\nReturn the extracted data along with the response:\n```javascript\nreturn {\n  llmResponse: naturalResponse,\n  treeAction: action?.action === 'tree_input' ? action.value : null,\n  extracted: action?.extracted || null,\n};\n```\n\n### Also fix the webhook route's else branch:\nWhen there's no treeAction, DON'T feed raw input to handleIncomingMessage. The LLM handled it — just send the LLM response. Only feed to tree engine if there IS a mapped action:\n\n```javascript\nif (treeAction) {\n  const treeResponses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, treeAction);\n  if (llmResponse) {\n    await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, llmResponse);\n  }\n} else if (llmResponse) {\n  // LLM handled it — DO NOT feed raw input to tree engine\n  // Just send the LLM response\n  await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, llmResponse);\n} else {\n  // LLM failed — fallback to tree engine\n  const responses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, input);\n  for (const response of responses) {\n    await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, response);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing:\nAfter making changes:\n1. Restart biomed-borbor: `pm2 restart biomed-borbor --update-env`\n2. Clear the test data: run `node -e \"const Database = require('better-sqlite3'); const db = new Database('data/medtech.db'); db.exec('DELETE FROM issues'); db.exec('DELETE FROM conversations'); db.exec('DELETE FROM technicians'); db.exec('DELETE FROM sqlite_sequence'); console.log('Cleared')\"`\n3. Check logs for any startup errors: `pm2 logs biomed-borbor --lines 20 --nostream`\n4. Verify the server is running: `curl http://localhost:3000/health`\n\n## IMPORTANT:\n- Don't break the existing LLM conversation quality — it's great\n- The tree engine still handles state transitions — just don't let it store bad data\n- The syncExtractedData function is a SUPPLEMENT, not a replacement\n- Keep the fuzzy matching in conversationEngine.js for when LLM is down (fallback mode)\n- Export syncExtractedData from llm-conversation.js or create a new data-sync.js service\n- Make sure the JSON extraction is robust — the LLM might not always return perfect JSON on the first line"}],"timestamp":1769989298949}}
{"type":"message","id":"c8ea0037","parentId":"0f4af4a0","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:42.019Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me read the current files to understand the codebase.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_016Szh3hGrFuFatVu6ZXzyhQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/src/services/llm-conversation.js"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FRNTXQVy2ztZoXygCo7zSc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/src/routes/webhook.js"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":3,"output":165,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":13215,"totalTokens":13383,"cost":{"input":0.000015000000000000002,"output":0.004125,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.08259375000000001,"total":0.08673375000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769989298950}}
{"type":"message","id":"be9fa8c4","parentId":"c8ea0037","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:42.047Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_016Szh3hGrFuFatVu6ZXzyhQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/**\n * LLM Conversation Layer for Biomed BorBor\n * \n * Wraps the structured troubleshooting engine with natural language.\n * The decision tree provides the correct diagnostic path;\n * the LLM makes it feel like talking to a knowledgeable colleague.\n * \n * Flow:\n *   User message → LLM interprets intent → maps to tree action → \n *   LLM wraps tree response in natural language → sends to user\n */\n\nconst Anthropic = require('@anthropic-ai/sdk').default;\nconst { getDb } = require('../models/db');\nconst { getTree, getAllTrees, getNode } = require('./troubleshootingTrees');\n\nconst client = new Anthropic({\n  apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,\n});\n\nconst MODEL = 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514';\nconst MAX_TOKENS = 500;\n\n// Conversation memory (in-memory, keyed by phone)\nconst conversationMemory = new Map();\n\nfunction getMemory(phone) {\n  if (!conversationMemory.has(phone)) {\n    conversationMemory.set(phone, { messages: [], lastActivity: Date.now() });\n  }\n  const mem = conversationMemory.get(phone);\n  mem.lastActivity = Date.now();\n  // Keep last 20 messages to control costs\n  if (mem.messages.length > 20) {\n    mem.messages = mem.messages.slice(-20);\n  }\n  return mem;\n}\n\nfunction addToMemory(phone, role, content) {\n  const mem = getMemory(phone);\n  mem.messages.push({ role, content });\n}\n\n// Clean up old conversations (>2 hours)\nsetInterval(() => {\n  const cutoff = Date.now() - 2 * 60 * 60 * 1000;\n  for (const [phone, mem] of conversationMemory) {\n    if (mem.lastActivity < cutoff) conversationMemory.delete(phone);\n  }\n}, 30 * 60 * 1000);\n\n/**\n * Get technician context for the system prompt\n */\nfunction getTechContext(phone) {\n  const db = getDb();\n  const tech = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM technicians WHERE phone = ?').get(phone);\n  if (!tech) return { name: null, facility: null, language: 'en', issueCount: 0 };\n\n  let facilityName = null;\n  if (tech.facility_id) {\n    const fac = db.prepare('SELECT name FROM facilities WHERE id = ?').get(tech.facility_id);\n    facilityName = fac?.name;\n  }\n\n  const issueCount = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) as c FROM issues WHERE technician_id = ?').get(tech.id).c;\n  const recentIssues = db.prepare(\n    'SELECT equipment_type, equipment_brand, resolution, resolved, started_at FROM issues WHERE technician_id = ? ORDER BY started_at DESC LIMIT 5'\n  ).all(tech.id);\n\n  return {\n    name: tech.name,\n    facility: facilityName,\n    language: tech.language || 'en',\n    issueCount,\n    recentIssues,\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Get current conversation state\n */\nfunction getConvState(phone) {\n  const db = getDb();\n  const conv = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM conversations WHERE phone = ?').get(phone);\n  if (!conv) return { state: 'idle', ctx: {} };\n  return { state: conv.state, ctx: JSON.parse(conv.context || '{}'), issueId: conv.current_issue_id };\n}\n\n/**\n * Build available equipment list\n */\nfunction getEquipmentList() {\n  const trees = getAllTrees();\n  return Object.values(trees).map(t => ({\n    id: t.id,\n    name: t.name,\n    brands: t.brands || [],\n  }));\n}\n\n/**\n * Get current troubleshooting node info\n */\nfunction getCurrentNodeInfo(phone) {\n  const convState = getConvState(phone);\n  if (convState.state !== 'troubleshooting' || !convState.ctx.treeId) return null;\n\n  const tree = getTree(convState.ctx.treeId);\n  if (!tree) return null;\n\n  const node = tree.nodes[convState.ctx.currentNode];\n  if (!node) return null;\n\n  return {\n    treeId: convState.ctx.treeId,\n    treeName: tree.name,\n    brand: convState.ctx.brand,\n    nodeId: convState.ctx.currentNode,\n    nodeText: node.text,\n    nodeType: node.type,\n    options: node.options ? Object.keys(node.options) : [],\n    parts: node.parts || [],\n    escalate: node.escalate || false,\n    stepCount: convState.ctx.stepCount || 0,\n    path: convState.ctx.path || [],\n  };\n}\n\n/**\n * Build PM schedule info for equipment\n */\nfunction getPMInfo(equipmentType) {\n  const pmSchedules = {\n    oxygen_concentrator: {\n      daily: ['Check flow rate output', 'Listen for unusual sounds', 'Check alarm indicators'],\n      weekly: ['Clean/replace intake filter', 'Check tubing connections', 'Wipe exterior surfaces'],\n      monthly: ['Inspect power cord', 'Check oxygen purity if analyzer available', 'Test all alarms'],\n      quarterly: ['Replace intake filter', 'Check internal air filter', 'Inspect compressor mount'],\n      annually: ['Replace sieve beds (or per manufacturer hours)', 'Full internal cleaning', 'Replace all filters'],\n    },\n    patient_monitor: {\n      daily: ['Visual inspection of screen and cables', 'Verify alarm settings', 'Check battery charge level'],\n      weekly: ['Clean SpO2 probes', 'Check ECG lead integrity', 'Clean screen with soft cloth'],\n      monthly: ['NIBP calibration check', 'Test all alarm functions', 'Inspect all cable connections'],\n      quarterly: ['Full battery cycle (discharge and recharge)', 'Calibrate temperature probe', 'Update software if available'],\n      annually: ['Full biomedical safety test', 'Replace NIBP cuff if worn', 'Replace disposable accessories'],\n    },\n    infant_incubator: {\n      daily: ['Verify temperature accuracy with calibrated thermometer', 'Check humidity levels', 'Inspect mattress and porthole seals'],\n      weekly: ['Clean water reservoir', 'Check fan operation', 'Inspect heater element visually'],\n      monthly: ['Calibrate temperature sensor', 'Deep clean interior', 'Check all alarms', 'Inspect power cord'],\n      quarterly: ['Replace air filter', 'Test skin temperature probe', 'Inspect door latches and hinges'],\n      annually: ['Full electrical safety test', 'Replace humidity system gaskets', 'Calibrate all sensors'],\n    },\n    autoclave: {\n      daily: ['Check water level', 'Inspect door gasket/seal', 'Run Bowie-Dick test (if applicable)'],\n      weekly: ['Clean chamber interior', 'Check drain screen/filter', 'Inspect trays and racks'],\n      monthly: ['Run biological indicator test', 'Check safety valve', 'Inspect heating elements'],\n      quarterly: ['Replace door gasket if worn', 'Descale chamber (if hard water)', 'Test pressure gauge calibration'],\n      annually: ['Full pressure vessel inspection', 'Replace safety valve', 'Professional calibration'],\n    },\n    centrifuge: {\n      daily: ['Check rotor seating', 'Listen for unusual vibration', 'Verify speed setting accuracy'],\n      weekly: ['Clean rotor and buckets', 'Inspect lid interlock', 'Check rubber cushions'],\n      monthly: ['Lubricate lid hinge', 'Check timer accuracy', 'Inspect power cord and plug'],\n      quarterly: ['Check speed calibration with tachometer', 'Inspect motor brushes', 'Clean interior thoroughly'],\n      annually: ['Full electrical safety test', 'Replace motor brushes if worn', 'Professional speed calibration'],\n    },\n    suction_machine: {\n      daily: ['Empty and clean canister', 'Check tubing for cracks', 'Verify suction pressure'],\n      weekly: ['Replace/clean bacterial filter', 'Check all connections for leaks', 'Clean exterior'],\n      monthly: ['Test overflow protection', 'Inspect diaphragm/pump', 'Check power cord'],\n      quarterly: ['Replace tubing', 'Test maximum suction level', 'Clean or replace intake filter'],\n      annually: ['Full electrical safety test', 'Replace diaphragm if applicable', 'Professional calibration'],\n    },\n  };\n\n  return pmSchedules[equipmentType] || null;\n}\n\n/**\n * Build system prompt\n */\nfunction buildSystemPrompt(phone) {\n  const tech = getTechContext(phone);\n  const convState = getConvState(phone);\n  const nodeInfo = getCurrentNodeInfo(phone);\n  const equipment = getEquipmentList();\n\n  let systemPrompt = `You are Biomed BorBor, a friendly and knowledgeable biomedical equipment troubleshooting assistant for health facilities in Sierra Leone and Liberia.\n\nPERSONALITY:\n- You're like a experienced senior biomedical technician texting with a colleague\n- Warm, encouraging, patient — but technically precise\n- Use simple language. These are busy techs, not reading essays.\n- Keep messages SHORT — 2-4 sentences max unless explaining a procedure\n- Sprinkle in Krio naturally if the tech speaks it (e.g., \"Kusheh!\" for greeting, \"Ow di bodi?\" for how are you)\n- Use emojis sparingly but naturally (🔧 ⚡ ✅ ⚠️)\n- NEVER give advice that could compromise patient safety, electrical safety, or infection control\n- If unsure, say so and recommend escalating to a senior technician\n\nCAPABILITIES:\n- Troubleshoot: ${equipment.map(e => e.name).join(', ')}\n- Preventative maintenance schedules for all equipment\n- Cross-facility learning (share fixes between facilities)\n- Log issues and track repair history\n\nAVAILABLE EQUIPMENT FOR TROUBLESHOOTING:\n${equipment.map((e, i) => `${i + 1}. ${e.name}${e.brands?.length ? ` (brands: ${e.brands.join(', ')})` : ''}`).join('\\n')}`;\n\n  if (tech.name) {\n    systemPrompt += `\\n\\nTECHNICIAN:\n- Name: ${tech.name}\n- Facility: ${tech.facility || 'Not set'}\n- Language: ${tech.language}\n- Issues logged: ${tech.issueCount}`;\n\n    if (tech.recentIssues?.length > 0) {\n      systemPrompt += `\\n- Recent issues: ${tech.recentIssues.map(i => \n        `${i.equipment_type}${i.equipment_brand ? ' (' + i.equipment_brand + ')' : ''} - ${i.resolved ? 'resolved' : 'open'}`\n      ).join('; ')}`;\n    }\n  } else {\n    systemPrompt += `\\n\\nNEW USER — needs to register (name, facility). Be extra welcoming.`;\n  }\n\n  if (convState.state === 'troubleshooting' && nodeInfo) {\n    systemPrompt += `\\n\\nACTIVE TROUBLESHOOTING SESSION:\n- Equipment: ${nodeInfo.treeName}${nodeInfo.brand ? ' (' + nodeInfo.brand + ')' : ''}\n- Step: ${nodeInfo.stepCount + 1}\n- Current diagnostic question: \"${nodeInfo.nodeText}\"\n- Valid responses: ${nodeInfo.options.length > 0 ? nodeInfo.options.join(', ') : 'free text'}\n${nodeInfo.escalate ? '⚠️ This may need escalation to a senior tech' : ''}\n${nodeInfo.parts.length > 0 ? '🔧 Parts that may be needed: ' + nodeInfo.parts.join(', ') : ''}\n\nIMPORTANT: Your job is to relay the diagnostic question naturally, but DO NOT skip steps or invent diagnoses. The troubleshooting tree is clinically validated. Rephrase the question conversationally, explain WHY we're asking if helpful, but always get the answer to THIS specific question.`;\n  } else {\n    systemPrompt += `\\n\\nCURRENT STATE: ${convState.state}\nThe tech can:\n1. Report an equipment problem (start troubleshooting)\n2. Ask about preventative maintenance schedules\n3. Check their issue history (\"status\")\n4. Change language\n5. Ask general biomedical equipment questions`;\n  }\n\n  // Add PM knowledge\n  systemPrompt += `\\n\\nPREVENTATIVE MAINTENANCE:\nIf a tech asks about PM, maintenance schedules, or routine checks, provide the schedule for their equipment. You know PM schedules for all supported equipment types. Be specific about frequencies (daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly/annual).`;\n\n  systemPrompt += `\\n\\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\n- Keep messages under 300 characters when possible (WhatsApp readability)\n- Use line breaks for clarity\n- For troubleshooting steps, number the options clearly\n- Always end with a clear question or call to action\n- If the tech seems frustrated, acknowledge it and encourage them`;\n\n  return systemPrompt;\n}\n\n/**\n * Main LLM conversation handler\n * Returns: { llmResponse: string, treeAction: string|null }\n * \n * treeAction tells the caller what to feed to the original conversation engine:\n *   - null: LLM handled it entirely (greetings, PM questions, etc.)\n *   - string: feed this to handleIncomingMessage as the \"input\"\n */\nasync function processWithLLM(phone, userMessage) {\n  const mem = getMemory(phone);\n  const convState = getConvState(phone);\n  const nodeInfo = getCurrentNodeInfo(phone);\n\n  // Add user message to memory\n  addToMemory(phone, 'user', userMessage);\n\n  const systemPrompt = buildSystemPrompt(phone);\n\n  // Determine if this is a PM question\n  const pmKeywords = ['maintenance', 'preventive', 'preventative', 'pm schedule', 'routine check', \n    'how often', 'cleaning schedule', 'filter replace', 'calibration', 'service schedule'];\n  const isPMQuestion = pmKeywords.some(kw => userMessage.toLowerCase().includes(kw));\n\n  // Build messages for LLM\n  const messages = [];\n  \n  // Add conversation memory\n  for (const msg of mem.messages) {\n    messages.push({ role: msg.role, content: msg.content });\n  }\n\n  // If in troubleshooting, add context about what we need from the user\n  if (convState.state === 'troubleshooting' && nodeInfo) {\n    // We need the LLM to:\n    // 1. Understand the user's response\n    // 2. Map it to one of the valid tree options\n    // 3. Respond naturally\n    \n    messages.push({\n      role: 'user',\n      content: `[SYSTEM: The user just said \"${userMessage}\" in response to the diagnostic question \"${nodeInfo.nodeText}\". Valid options are: ${nodeInfo.options.join(', ')}. \n      \nYour task: \n1. Determine which option best matches their response (or if they're asking something else)\n2. Respond naturally and conversationally\n3. Start your response with a JSON line: {\"action\": \"tree_input\", \"value\": \"<matched option>\"} or {\"action\": \"none\"} if it's not a tree response\n4. Then on the next line, your natural response to the user]`\n    });\n  } else if (isPMQuestion) {\n    // Handle PM questions directly with LLM\n    const equipMatch = Object.keys(getAllTrees()).find(id => {\n      const tree = getTree(id);\n      return userMessage.toLowerCase().includes(tree.name.toLowerCase()) || \n             userMessage.toLowerCase().includes(id.replace('_', ' '));\n    });\n\n    if (equipMatch) {\n      const pmInfo = getPMInfo(equipMatch);\n      if (pmInfo) {\n        const tree = getTree(equipMatch);\n        messages[messages.length - 1] = {\n          role: 'user',\n          content: `[SYSTEM: User is asking about preventative maintenance for ${tree.name}. Here is the PM schedule:\\n${JSON.stringify(pmInfo, null, 2)}\\n\\nRespond naturally with the relevant PM info. Start with {\"action\": \"none\"} on the first line.]`\n        };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const response = await client.messages.create({\n      model: MODEL,\n      max_tokens: MAX_TOKENS,\n      system: systemPrompt,\n      messages,\n    });\n\n    const fullResponse = response.content[0]?.text || '';\n    \n    // Parse action line\n    let action = null;\n    let naturalResponse = fullResponse;\n\n    const firstLine = fullResponse.split('\\n')[0];\n    try {\n      if (firstLine.startsWith('{')) {\n        action = JSON.parse(firstLine);\n        naturalResponse = fullResponse.substring(firstLine.length).trim();\n      }\n    } catch {\n      // No action line, full response is natural language\n    }\n\n    // Add assistant response to memory\n    addToMemory(phone, 'assistant', naturalResponse);\n\n    return {\n      llmResponse: naturalResponse,\n      treeAction: action?.action === 'tree_input' ? action.value : null,\n    };\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('❌ LLM error:', err.message);\n    // Fallback: return null so the original engine handles it\n    return { llmResponse: null, treeAction: null };\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { processWithLLM, getPMInfo };\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1769989302045}}
{"type":"message","id":"fa3630c4","parentId":"be9fa8c4","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:42.051Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01FRNTXQVy2ztZoXygCo7zSc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const express = require('express');\nconst router = express.Router();\nconst { handleIncomingMessage, handlePhoto } = require('../services/conversationEngine');\nconst { sendCloudApiMessage } = require('../services/whatsapp-cloud');\nconst { processWithLLM } = require('../services/llm-conversation');\n\n// Webhook verification (GET)\nrouter.get('/', (req, res) => {\n  const mode = req.query['hub.mode'];\n  const token = req.query['hub.verify_token'];\n  const challenge = req.query['hub.challenge'];\n\n  if (mode === 'subscribe' && token === process.env.WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN) {\n    console.log('✅ Webhook verified');\n    return res.status(200).send(challenge);\n  }\n  res.sendStatus(403);\n});\n\n// Incoming messages (POST)\nrouter.post('/', async (req, res) => {\n  // Always respond 200 quickly to avoid retries\n  res.sendStatus(200);\n\n  try {\n    const body = req.body;\n    if (!body.object) return;\n\n    const entries = body.entry || [];\n    for (const entry of entries) {\n      const changes = entry.changes || [];\n      for (const change of changes) {\n        if (change.field !== 'messages') continue;\n        const value = change.value;\n        if (!value.messages) continue;\n\n        for (const message of value.messages) {\n          const from = message.from;\n\n          // Handle image messages\n          if (message.type === 'image' && message.image?.id) {\n            console.log(`📷 Image from ${from}, media ID: ${message.image.id}`);\n            const responses = await handlePhoto(from, message.image.id);\n            for (const response of responses) {\n              await sendCloudApiMessage(from, response);\n            }\n            continue;\n          }\n\n          // Handle text and interactive messages\n          const text = message.type === 'text' ? message.text.body : null;\n          const interactive = message.type === 'interactive'\n            ? (message.interactive.button_reply?.id || message.interactive.list_reply?.id)\n            : null;\n          const input = text || interactive;\n          if (!input) continue;\n\n          console.log(`📨 Message from ${from}: ${input}`);\n\n          // Use LLM-powered conversation if API key is set\n          if (process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) {\n            await handleWithLLM(from, input);\n          } else {\n            // Fallback to original tree-based engine\n            const responses = await handleIncomingMessage(from, input);\n            for (const response of responses) {\n              await sendCloudApiMessage(from, response);\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('❌ Webhook error:', err);\n  }\n});\n\n/**\n * Handle message with LLM layer.\n * The LLM interprets the user's natural language,\n * feeds appropriate actions to the tree engine,\n * and wraps responses in conversational language.\n */\nasync function handleWithLLM(phone, input) {\n  try {\n    // Step 1: Let LLM process the message\n    const { llmResponse, treeAction } = await processWithLLM(phone, input);\n\n    // Step 2: If LLM identified a tree action, feed it to the engine\n    if (treeAction) {\n      // Feed the mapped action to the structured engine\n      const treeResponses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, treeAction);\n      \n      // Send the LLM's natural response (which contextualizes the tree's next step)\n      if (llmResponse) {\n        await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, llmResponse);\n      }\n      \n      // If the tree produced important structured output (like a summary),\n      // send that too — but only if LLM didn't already cover it\n      // Skip sending raw tree responses since LLM handles the conversation\n      \n    } else if (llmResponse) {\n      // LLM handled it entirely (greetings, PM questions, general questions)\n      // But still feed to tree engine for state management\n      const treeResponses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, input);\n      \n      // Send LLM response instead of tree response\n      await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, llmResponse);\n      \n    } else {\n      // LLM failed — fallback to tree engine\n      console.log('⚠️ LLM fallback — using tree engine directly');\n      const responses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, input);\n      for (const response of responses) {\n        await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, response);\n      }\n    }\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('❌ LLM handler error:', err.message);\n    // Always fallback to tree engine on error\n    try {\n      const responses = await handleIncomingMessage(phone, input);\n      for (const response of responses) {\n        await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, response);\n      }\n    } catch (fallbackErr) {\n      console.error('❌ Fallback also failed:', fallbackErr.message);\n      await sendCloudApiMessage(phone, \"Sorry, I'm having trouble right now. Please try again in a moment. 🙏\");\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = router;\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1769989302050}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8195e35","parentId":"fa3630c4","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:53.329Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I can see the exact bug. Let me implement the fixes."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JABUFVo9S9DAzjWXWC65W4","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/src/services/llm-conversation.js","oldText":"  systemPrompt += `\\n\\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\n- Keep messages under 300 characters when possible (WhatsApp readability)\n- Use line breaks for clarity\n- For troubleshooting steps, number the options clearly\n- Always end with a clear question or call to action\n- If the tech seems frustrated, acknowledge it and encourage them`;","newText":"  systemPrompt += `\\n\\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\nAlways start your response with a JSON line containing structured data extraction:\n{\"action\": \"tree_input\", \"value\": \"<matched option>\", \"extracted\": {\"name\": null, \"facility\": null, \"equipment_type\": null, \"brand\": null, \"symptom\": null, \"model\": null}}\n\nUse \"action\": \"tree_input\" with a \"value\" when the user's message maps to a tree option.\nUse \"action\": \"none\" when it doesn't map to any tree option (greetings, PM questions, general chat).\n\nThe \"extracted\" object should contain ANY information you can identify from the ENTIRE conversation so far:\n- name: the technician's name if they've mentioned it\n- facility: the health facility name\n- equipment_type: one of: oxygen concentrator, autoclave, centrifuge, infant incubator, patient monitor, suction machine\n- brand: equipment brand/manufacturer (DeVilbiss, AirSep, Longfian, Canta, BPL, Tuttnauer, Prestige Medical, Edan, etc.)\n- symptom: the main problem described (e.g., \"loud grinding noise\", \"won't start\", \"low oxygen output\")\n- model: specific model number if mentioned\nOnly include fields you're confident about. Use null for unknown fields.\n\nAfter the JSON line, write your natural response to the user.\n- Keep messages under 300 characters when possible (WhatsApp readability)\n- Use line breaks for clarity\n- For troubleshooting steps, number the options clearly\n- Always end with a clear question or call to action\n- If the tech seems frustrated, acknowledge it and encourage them`;"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":604,"cacheRead":13215,"cacheWrite":6035,"totalTokens":19855,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.0151,"cacheRead":0.0066075,"cacheWrite":0.03771875,"total":0.059431250000000005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769989302051}}
{"type":"message","id":"68ecc432","parentId":"d8195e35","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:41:53.354Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01JABUFVo9S9DAzjWXWC65W4","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced text in /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/medtech-bot/src/services/llm-conversation.js."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 250   systemPrompt += `\\n\\nPREVENTATIVE MAINTENANCE:\n 251 If a tech asks about PM, maintenance schedules, or routine checks, provide the schedule for their equipment. You know PM schedules for all supported equipment types. Be specific about frequencies (daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly/annual).`;\n 252 \n 253   systemPrompt += `\\n\\nRESPONSE FORMAT:\n+254 Always start your response with a JSON line containing structured data extraction:\n+255 {\"action\": \"tree_input\", \"value\": \"<matched option>\", \"extracted\": {\"name\": null, \"facility\": null, \"equipment_type\": null, \"brand\": null, \"symptom\": null, \"model\": null}}\n+256 \n+257 Use \"action\": \"tree_input\" with a \"value\" when the user's message maps to a tree option.\n+258 Use \"action\": \"none\" when it doesn't map to any tree option (greetings, PM questions, general chat).\n+259 \n+260 The \"extracted\" object should contain ANY information you can identify from the ENTIRE conversation so far:\n+261 - name: the technician's name if they've mentioned it\n+262 - facility: the health facility name\n+263 - equipment_type: one of: oxygen concentrator, autoclave, centrifuge, infant incubator, patient monitor, suction machine\n+264 - brand: equipment brand/manufacturer (DeVilbiss, AirSep, Longfian, Canta, BPL, Tuttnauer, Prestige Medical, Edan, etc.)\n+265 - symptom: the main problem described (e.g., \"loud grinding noise\", \"won't start\", \"low oxygen output\")\n+266 - model: specific model number if mentioned\n+267 Only include fields you're confident about. Use null for unknown fields.\n+268 \n+269 After the JSON line, write your natural response to the user.\n 254 - Keep messages under 300 characters when possible (WhatsApp readability)\n 255 - Use line breaks for clarity\n 256 - For troubleshooting steps, number the options clearly\n 257 - Always end with a clear question or call to action\n     ...","firstChangedLine":254},"isError":false,"timestamp":1769989313353}}
