{"type":"message","id":"c2b68cde","parentId":"53df3a0c","timestamp":"2026-02-01T23:42:39.747Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Here's what I fixed:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/services/llm-conversation.js`:**\n   - Updated the system prompt's RESPONSE FORMAT to instruct the LLM to always return an `extracted` object with structured fields (`name`, `facility`, `equipment_type`, `brand`, `symptom`, `model`) alongside every response\n   - Modified `processWithLLM` to return the `extracted` data from the LLM's JSON response\n   - Added `syncExtractedData(phone, extracted)` function that directly updates the DB (technicians table for name/facility, issues table for equipment_type/brand/symptom/model), bypassing the tree engine's state machine\n   - Exported `syncExtractedData`\n\n2. **`src/routes/webhook.js`:**\n   - Imported `syncExtractedData`\n   - Modified `handleWithLLM` to call `syncExtractedData` after every LLM response (with error handling so sync failures are non-fatal)\n   - **Critical fix:** Removed the `else if (llmResponse)` branch that was feeding raw user input to `handleIncomingMessage` — now it just sends the LLM response without touching the tree engine, preventing misclassified data storage\n\nServer restarted cleanly, health check passes."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":311,"cacheRead":24571,"cacheWrite":140,"totalTokens":25023,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.007775000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0122855,"cacheWrite":0.000875,"total":0.0209405}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1769989351828}}
